# Sandcastle spike: per-repo sandbox scaffold/scratch (Dockerfile, .env, logs,
# worktrees) created by `sandcastle init` at the repo root. Spike-local; never
# commit (the .env there holds the OpenAI key).
.sandcastle/
.next/
.turbo/
dist/
# EXCEPTION: the Paperclip plugins' built dist/ IS committed. The Droplet
# deploy ships the tree via `git archive` (committed files only) and bind-mounts
# the plugins as prebuilt artifacts (they are NOT built on the Droplet), so the
# manifest + worker bundles must be in git or Paperclip can't activate them
# ("no longer exposes a Paperclip manifest"). Rebuild after editing plugin src:
#   pnpm --filter @agenticos/<name>-plugin run build
#
# DECISION, GOL-2694 (2026-09-30) — "stop committing dist and build on the
# droplet instead" was considered and REJECTED. Please don't re-litigate it
# without changing one of these facts:
#   * the deploy ships `git archive` output, which is committed files ONLY, so
#     an uncommitted dist simply would not reach the box;
#   * the plugins are deliberately not built on the droplet. Moving the build
#     there converts a red CI check into a live plugin-layer outage whenever an
#     install or an esbuild run fails on a 2-vCPU box — strictly worse blast
#     radius for the thing that runs the company's automation;
#   * the recurring cost that motivated the question (every dependency bump
#     rewriting the committed bundles) was removed at the source instead, by
#     normalizing the pnpm store paths out of the esbuild output — see
#     scripts/normalize-plugin-bundle.mjs.
# Revisit only if the deploy path stops using `git archive` AND the droplet
# gains a build toolchain whose failure modes are alerted on.
!packages/vault-plugin/dist/
!packages/openviking-plugin/dist/
!packages/github-plugin/dist/
!packages/github-sync-plugin/dist/
!packages/grove-content-drafter-plugin/dist/
build/
out/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
.DS_Store
# macOS Finder/iCloud Drive copy-on-conflict artifacts.
# Pattern: any path like "watcher 2.py" or "Dockerfile 3" — Finder/iCloud
# appends " N" (with leading space) before any extension when it detects a
# sibling already at the same path. Purely a sync-collision artifact, never
# source. Globs cover both with-extension (* 2.*) and bare (* 2) cases.
* [234].*
* [234]
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.log
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo

